    "body": "This should cover all the existing support from the autoconf/Make build:\n* building tools/\n* building and running tests\n* generating and install the man pages\n* installing the library / header files\n* regenerating the static test files based on existing terminfo files",
    "closed_at": "2026-08-27T10:18:45Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I'll re-run Neovim CI on these changes and make a new release if they pass.\r\n\r\n\r\n**EDIT:** They don't, because the Zig build scripts also need updating. Not an issue with this repo, but this raises the question whether we want to upstream the (fixed) Zig scripts?",
